cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use intronfate, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "intronfate"
abstract: >-
  Projects annotated introns from GFF3/GTF files onto protein alignments as (alignment column, phase) positions,
  builds an intron presence/absence/missing matrix across genomes, and reconstructs intron gain and loss on a
  species tree (Dollo and Fitch parsimony, weighted Dollo, and a likelihood model with annotation error).
  Reads and writes MALIN intron tables.
authors:
  - family-names: Stajich
    given-names: "Jason E."
    affiliation: University of California-Riverside
    email: jason.stajich@ucr.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7591-0020"
repository-code: "https://github.com/stajichlab/intronfate"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
# date-released: TODO (set when the release is tagged)
# doi: TODO (Zenodo archive of the tagged release)
keywords:
  - introns
  - comparative genomics
  - molecular evolution
  - Dollo parsimony
  - Rust
